    "bottomLine": "The Lectric XP 4.0 Step-Thru gives you certification, a torque sensor and hydraulic brakes for about $1,000, in a frame that folds."
  },
  {
    "id": "lectric-xp-trike-2",
    "name": "Lectric XP Trike 2",
    "badge": "Best Trike",
    "category": "Folding Electric Trike",
    "description": "The Lectric XP Trike 2 is the trike to look at if balance is your main concern and you want to keep the cost down. Freshly Charged lists it at $1,499, with a 500 W, 65 Nm motor and a 624 Wh battery, and Lectric claims up to 50 miles of range, though Freshly Charged expects 30 to 40 miles in everyday riding. It folds, which is unusual for a trike and helps with storage and transport. It is heavy: the claimed weight is 86 pounds and Electric Bike Report measured its test bike at 91.1 pounds, while Freshly Charged lists 79 pounds without the battery. The original XP Trike was described by Electrek as easy to mount with a low step-through frame and sizing for riders from 4 feet 10 inches to 6 feet 4 inches; confirm the sizing for the current model. As with any trike, take corners slowly and practice in a quiet space first.",
    "pros": [
      "Three wheels: stays upright at stops",
      "Folds for storage, unusual for a trike",
      "500 W, 65 Nm motor and 624 Wh battery",
      "About $1,499 per Freshly Charged"
    ],
    "cons": [
      "Claimed 86 lb; measured 91.1 lb by Electric Bike Report",
      "Wide; needs garage or shed space",
      "Corners require care, as with all trikes"
    ],
    "bottomLine": "For riders who want three-wheel stability without spending a fortune, the folding Lectric XP Trike 2 is the most practical starting point."
  },
  {
