          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            The best electric bike for most older riders is the Aventon Pace 4 Step-Through, which combines a low frame, smooth torque-sensing assist and light-touch hydraulic brakes. The Lectric XP 4.0 Step-Thru delivers certification and a torque sensor for about $1,000, and riders who want three-wheel stability should start with the Lectric XP Trike 2 or Rad RadTrike.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Whatever you choose, prioritize a truly low step-through frame, start in the lowest assist level, insist on a certified battery and the supplied charger, wear a helmet, and talk to your doctor if you have health concerns. Those choices matter more than top speed or range.
          </p>
